  "result": "The gate never actually checked my work: both runs came back `SCOPE_VIOLATION`, triggered by files the agent runtime creates, not by the two concept files. I stopped after 2 of the 6 runs because every further run would fail the same way.\n\n**Why the gate fails:** each shell command I run makes the runtime write an output file under `.runtime/tmp/...` inside the repository. The gate treats that as a change outside the concept's files. On the second run, with nothing else changed, it reported a different file, the one created by that run's own command. I can't delete these files, since the gate is the only command I'm allowed to run. To get a real verdict, the harness needs to:\n- re-run the gate from outside this session (it plans to do this after I stop),\n- ignore `.runtime/tmp`, or\n- move the agent's temp folder out of the worktree.\n\n**What I wrote:**\n- **Concept** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/moving_backward.lean`): the body is `vx·hx + vy·hy < −speed_tol`, using the x and y parts of `kin_velocity` and `kin_heading` (the evaluator scales the heading to unit length). The comparison is strict, so a value of exactly −speed_tol doesn't count as moving backward. If either vector is missing, the result is unknown.\n- **Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/motion/moving_backward.lean`): speed_tol is 0.1 m/s, with one car heading east over three scenes 1 s apart:\n  - **holds:** velocity (−1.5, 0), with the position moving west to match.\n  - **fails:** velocity (2.0, 0.1), with the position moving to match.\n  - **blind:** same as holds, but with no velocity and `kin.velocity` masked.\n\nThe contract left nothing open, so I declared no narrowings. The record looks sound.\n\n`task_result.md` in the working directory has the full report.",
